=== FINDINGS ===
F1 (acceptance 3, brief-level, NOT a work defect): acceptance 3 as literally
   written ("multiset of trimmed TEXT NODES identical except +Period details
   / -Data freshness") cannot be satisfied by any implementation of section
   A.1, because A.1 itself mandates concatenating the "Latest transaction: …"
   / "No transaction data available." sentence into the "Selected period: …"
   text node with " · ". Two master text nodes therefore become one. Exact
   divergence is quoted above. Same class as ruling LT-2026-09-07a (the
   structural section is authoritative; the derived acceptance number was an
   estimate). Sentence-level parity — the property the criterion exists to
   protect, "every sentence still exists" (LT.0) — holds exactly, on all four
   fixtures. Recommend the lead record a ruling rather than reopen LT1.
F2 (process, no code impact): `scripts/whatif-verify.sh start 8101` reported
   "Instance already running on :8101 — stopping it first". Another checker
   (likely the a11y lane) may have had a server on that port; I restarted it
   from my scratch tree and stopped it when done.

